1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,740
Time to partner up, class. I want you to hold hands when you've found your one, okay?

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,980
Hey, wanna be with me?

3
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:09,840
Sure.

4
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:12,500
Has everybody paired off?

5
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,940
Seems we have an odd man out.

6
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:19,880
Hey, kids, who wants Miyamura to be their second partner?

7
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:21,060
No way.

8
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:23,720
He's gross. And really weird, too.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,780
We'll be conducting an experiment.

10
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,700
But before we do anything, break into groups of five.

11
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:38,220
And melancholy Miyamura's solo yet again.

12
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:41,020
Like, I can never get a solid weed on that guy.

13
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:43,260
Hey! Someone take the leftover!

14
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:55,640
Yep. About sums it up.

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:11,840
School's pretty tough. In lots of ways.

16
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:18,460
If they gave out an award for Most Depressing Kid, he'd win every year.

17
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:21,120
Wait, who would?

18
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:22,300
Miyamura, duh.

19
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:25,460
I don't think I know that name.

20
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,180
Seriously? Where have you been? Under a rock?

21
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:32,760
I heard we're supposed to team up in roster order for this next classics report.

22
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:34,580
What are you doing?

23
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:35,080
Nothing.

24
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:38,760
Nothing.

25
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:41,880
I saw you hide something, though.

26
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,100
Apparently, we're grouped up next project.

27
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:47,460
Oh, um, that's news to me.

28
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:49,080
So, uh...

29
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,000
Do you not know my name?

30
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:52,440
I feel like you should this late in the year, but it's Hori.

31
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,120
I'm sorry.

32
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:58,360
Huh? I could've sworn she told those girls she didn't know my name, either.

33
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,480
Anyway, people say you're kinda gloomy.

34
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:03,340
Oh, yeah?

35
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:05,380
I talked to you so I could see for myself.

36
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,540
And I don't get it.

37
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:10,480
Cause you seem totally normal to me.

38
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:16,120
This Hori girl...

39
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:18,480
Is kinda weird.

40
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:48,460
I mean...

41
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:50,480
Yeah

42
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:21,820
映り変わる季節模様

43
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:23,700
きっと消えない

44
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:25,420
今日は言えない

45
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:28,660
元通りにはもうできない

46
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:34,620
あの頃に隠した本物はどこ

47
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:36,420
怒ってくれない

48
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:38,020
わかってくれない

49
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:42,040
思ってもただ募ってしまうだけ

50
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:45,680
懐かしい匂いと

51
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:49,280
この歌が残る

52
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:49,340
この歌が残る

53
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:59,200
I found my name!

54
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:01,780
Looks like I'm gonna be in Class 1 with you, Yugi.

55
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:02,440
Awesome!

56
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:05,720
Class 1, Class 1, come on, Class 1.

57
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,840
You guys find your name yet?

58
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:08,420
Oh, I'm Class 1.

59
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:10,620
Yes, Class 1 for me too!

60
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:13,980
This just goes to show how strong the power of love can truly be.

61
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,280
It's fate!

62
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,540
Wait, love?

63
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:19,020
So because they're in the same class,

64
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,720
they have a faded love?

65
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,620
Is it a romance or are they dating?

66
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,420
Oh yeah!

67
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:26,260
We'll be together till we graduate!

68
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:28,740
You guys find your classes yet?

69
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,760
Yep, sure did.

70
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:32,700
Oh gosh!

71
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,320
I don't think it's worth crying over.

72
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:35,800
People are whispering.

73
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:37,820
Then grow up and do something!

74
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:39,220
Take it easy.

75
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:41,600
Hit him too hard and you might snap his poor spine.

76
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,060
True!

77
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,580
Oh yeah, Ishikawa.

78
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:45,420
Remember that song you gave me the other day?

79
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,920
I accidentally deleted it, so...

80
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:48,220
What?

81
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:49,060
Come on, dude.

82
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:52,700
Well, I was trying to free up some storage and then...

83
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:54,440
Sometimes I wonder...

84
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:55,260
Extra storage.

85
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:55,780
I did!

86
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:57,520
I just have a lot of stuff on it!

87
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:58,780
Even though I'm in this group,

88
00:04:59,580 --> 00:05:00,820
am I actually one of them?

89
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:01,840
Or not?

90
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,280
She doesn't need it!

91
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:05,500
Huh, you're making me want to hear it too.

92
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:10,060
Okay, I want everybody to split into groups of four for this next project.

93
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:11,500
Go ahead and team up now.

94
00:05:15,740 --> 00:05:17,500
Miyamura, you're all alone?

95
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:23,920
Yoshikawa, let me borrow a pen.

96
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:25,260
You had like a million last time I counted.

97
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,380
You can't even count that high.

98
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,800
And if you're going to be a bully about it, you don't get one.

99
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:30,740
Well, you suck.

100
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,140
Anybody pick up the packet yet?

101
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:34,800
Yeah, I have it.

102
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:38,320
Nice!

103
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:40,860
Turning the outline into a draft's all hoodie.

104
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:42,320
Need more paper?

105
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,120
Nah, we should be good.

106
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:46,560
Miyamura, you've got the chart, cool?

107
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:47,600
Oh, sure.

108
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:55,080
Honey!

109
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,820
Toru took my pen and he won't give it back!

110
00:05:58,060 --> 00:05:59,640
Cause I'm still using it, okay?

111
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:01,040
Knock it off, you two!

112
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:12,740
Friends.

113
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:16,660
Can I really call them that?

114
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:17,920
Are we friends?

115
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:21,040
Hard to wrap my head around.

116
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:25,140
I've been looking for you!

117
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:27,020
Everything cool?

118
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:29,760
Yeah, no big deal.

119
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:32,120
Our next class was just switched from math to econ.

120
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:35,500
I don't think I bought the textbook for that.

121
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:38,520
When they pull crap like this, it's so unfair.

122
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:40,580
Listen, man.

123
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,320
I gotta ask you something.

124
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:42,380
Okay.

125
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:52,620
So, yeah.

126
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,540
You got any helpful advice?

127
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:57,740
What?

128
00:06:58,680 --> 00:06:59,160
Wait!

129
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:00,820
Were you zoning out this whole time?

130
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:02,320
It's just...

131
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,120
I have a question, too.

132
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:05,320
Ishikawa.

133
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:09,580
What, um, what do you think of me?

134
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:15,840
Asking people that with a straight face is creepy as hell.

135
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:19,080
As if you getting close with Horty isn't annoying enough.

136
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:22,080
It's also frustrating how you never say what you mean.

137
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,260
And you're just plain weird.

138
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:28,600
You're also way too nice to people.

139
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:32,180
But the real kicker is when you lose the glasses and put your hair up,

140
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:33,960
you're prettier than most girls I know.

141
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:35,600
It takes me off.

142
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,040
So I'm a pretty boy?

143
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:42,520
That's another thing!

144
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:45,060
You make me say the dumbest shit without even realizing it,

145
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:46,440
and it drives me freaking crazy!

146
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:47,720
That's my fault?

147
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:50,080
If I'm being honest,

148
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:53,100
I guess I kind of wonder what you think of me too sometimes.

149
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:56,780
You're one of the few people who still calls me by my last name.

150
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,160
To-

151
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:01,640
To-

152
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:01,760
To-

153
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:01,820
To-

154
00:08:01,820 --> 00:08:01,960
To-

155
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:02,140
To-

156
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:02,200
To-

157
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:02,260
To-

158
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:03,940
To-

159
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:04,940
To-

160
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:05,940
To-

161
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:08,180
To-

162
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:08,880
The heck!

163
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:11,920
Don't say it if you're going to be all bashful afterward, dude!

164
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:13,300
I'm so sorry!

165
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,460
It just slipped out, but...

166
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:17,160
Um, truthfully...

167
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:19,160
Well...

168
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:26,820
The reason I acted so funny was because that was the first time in high school I called a classmate by their first name.

169
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:28,900
I swear

170
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:33,740
You're so weird

171
00:08:33,740 --> 00:08:45,860
Sorry

172
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:46,820
Don't apologize

173
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:49,660
I didn't say it was bad

174
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:52,680
Nothing wrong with being a little awkward

175
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:55,880
Ain't that right?

176
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:57,080
Izumi?

177
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,360
I'm okay

178
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:16,200
I wish I could go back in time ten years

179
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:18,000
And tell myself that

180
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:23,800
If you're gonna do a forehead flick

181
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:26,360
Hold back a little so you don't hit our skulls so hard

182
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:28,620
I said we'd finish the report over lunch

183
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:29,580
And you both bail

184
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:31,140
You better have a good reason

185
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:34,020
Is affirming our friendship on the roof a good reason?

186
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,240
You're both as creepy as you are stupid

187
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,300
If you're being serious

188
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:38,920
Hey, if we're stupid then

189
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:39,960
What does that make Yoshikawa?

190
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:41,960
And what is that supposed to mean?

191
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:52,860
Ah, hey

192
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:53,800
What's up, Ishikawa?

193
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:54,980
Sleep well?

194
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:55,240
Huh?

195
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:57,580
So

196
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:59,720
I watched that show you were raving about

197
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,240
Izumi

198
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:02,180
Maybe it's still too soon

199
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:03,660
But do you have a favorite part?

200
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,240
Let's see

201
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:07,260
And here I was

202
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:09,240
Thinking we were on a first name basis now

203
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:11,380
This guy's a total mystery

204
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:12,580
Did you hear me?

205
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:13,120
Hey

206
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,240
Ishikawa?

207
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:23,260
You done yet, sissy?

208
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:24,740
Time to go

209
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:26,220
What?

210
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,200
This early?

211
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:27,920
Yeah

212
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:29,000
Yuna's waiting on me

213
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:29,800
So hurry up

214
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:40,720
Sota's been getting up way earlier

215
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,780
Now that he's in grade school

216
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:43,300
Nobody's even here yet

217
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:46,600
The seat taken?

218
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:49,100
Oh

219
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:50,240
Hey, Ayasaki

220
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:53,080
Remy thought we had a morning assembly today

221
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,260
So she got here early

222
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:56,300
Yeah, same here

223
00:10:57,460 --> 00:11:03,040
So

224
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:05,960
That Miyamoto guy is pretty hot, huh?

225
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,420
Uh, is he?

226
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,140
Are you his girlfriend?

227
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,820
Cause he sure act like you are

228
00:11:10,820 --> 00:11:11,420
What?

229
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:12,180
Nuh-uh

230
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:13,060
Hmm

231
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:14,980
You don't say

232
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:17,120
Well, great

233
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,300
I guess that means Remy can have him then

234
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:21,380
Huh?

235
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:22,620
Sorry

236
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:24,140
Have?

237
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,640
Yeah, he's fair game

238
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:26,340
So why not?

239
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:27,220
I mean

240
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:29,080
I can get as close as I want to Miyamoto

241
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:29,800
If he's single

242
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,820
Shouldn't make any difference to you, right?

243
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:34,540
Well, uh

244
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:35,980
Yeah

245
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:36,800
Cool

246
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,380
Then Remy calls Dibs

247
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:38,420
Then Remy calls Dibs

248
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:42,480
No

249
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:43,820
Hmm?

250
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:45,260
There's no Dibs

251
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:46,460
He's mine

252
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:47,220
What?

253
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:48,540
Hold on

254
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:52,720
How can you claim someone when 30 seconds before you were even dating him?

255
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:53,640
I'm not giving him to you

256
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:54,820
Why not?

257
00:11:54,980 --> 00:11:56,180
Because I don't want to

258
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:57,020
That's why

259
00:11:57,020 --> 00:12:00,600
Remy asked if you're a Miyamoto's girlfriend and you said no

260
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,640
So he doesn't belong to you

261
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:04,380
I know what I said

262
00:12:04,380 --> 00:12:06,960
And now I'm saying you can't have him

263
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,060
Not ever

264
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,380
Do you hear me?

265
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:11,340
I'll never let you have him

266
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:14,300
I hope the cafeteria is open

267
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:21,340
Well, see ya

268
00:12:21,340 --> 00:12:33,140
I'm so stupid

269
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:35,680
Miyamoto doesn't belong to anyone

270
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:57,100
I should be used to these messes by now

271
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:57,760
But no

272
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:00,440
I don't care if Sota's in a rush to play

273
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:01,900
The living room is not his closet

274
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:06,900
Aw, Sota's M.I.A?

275
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:10,080
These days he only comes home to change for soccer

276
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:10,840
Sorry

277
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:14,020
That's a kid's stamina for ya

278
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:17,060
You can't do blueberries, right, Hori?

279
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:17,960
Hmm

280
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:21,780
Sota's been busier since he started grade school

281
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:25,100
So Miyamura and I spend a lot more time alone

282
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:28,900
That fruit tart you brought over the other day was really good

283
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:29,680
Oh yeah?

284
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:32,640
Believe it or not, that one was made by yours truly

285
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:35,080
Look at you, Mr. Talented

286
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:40,040
Sometimes

287
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:44,040
We just sort of stop talking

288
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:50,500
That looked way too real

289
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:51,620
Come on

290
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:53,240
It was totally special effects

291
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:55,720
I bet you're saying that because you're actually scared

292
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:57,460
And you just don't want to admit it, right?

293
00:13:57,460 --> 00:14:00,200
I know it's fake, because that stuff only happens in movies

294
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:03,440
Relax, Miyamura

295
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:05,340
That's the sound of a text, not a demon

296
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:09,800
Mom's gonna be late again, shocker

297
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:12,620
I'm so embarrassed

298
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:15,480
Blackout?

299
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:17,580
Hey, Hori

300
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:19,440
Where's your breaker box?

301
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:21,060
The lights will come back in a second

302
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:22,040
We're fine

303
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:23,540
You call this fine?

304
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:24,660
Wow

305
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:25,980
That was fast

306
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:28,860
This house is definitely cursed

307
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:32,380
The lights came back on, so what's with that face?

308
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,600
Better suck it up, because it's time for disc two

309
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,600
Disc two?

310
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,720
They made more of this awful franchise?

311
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,680
How many are there?

312
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,560
We're gonna watch the first three now

313
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:44,960
Then we'll do the last two when Sota gets home

314
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:47,520
What kind of torture is this?

315
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:51,460
Wow

316
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:53,760
She was right

317
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:55,100
You are double-jointed, huh?

318
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:55,660
Huh?

319
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:56,860
And your finger

320
00:14:56,860 --> 00:14:58,280
Oh

321
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:02,180
Your hands are tiny, Yuki

322
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:03,320
Ooh

323
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:05,520
Hey, Grabby

324
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:07,920
Doesn't your heart skip a beat when someone takes your hand?

325
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:08,680
I don't know

326
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:10,960
What I do know is you have the cutest little fingers

327
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:15,320
I bet your hands look little, too, when you compare them to a guy's

328
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:17,700
Guy's hands aren't near as fun to compare, though

329
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:22,380
Latch on and you're dead

330
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:25,460
You hear what she said, Miyamura?

331
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:29,720
I'm literally risking my life just for the chance to touch Hori's hand

332
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:31,400
Mine are open and waiting

333
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,020
You can touch away

334
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:33,880
No thanks

335
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:34,640
Wow

336
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:36,020
Your finger's double-jointed

337
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:37,240
That's so neat, Hori

338
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:39,240
It makes me unique

339
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,580
Did you break it when you were a kid or something?

340
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:42,700
No

341
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:44,500
I was born with it

342
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:48,580
How does that joint even work, though?

343
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:49,140
Huh

344
00:15:49,140 --> 00:15:51,900
I'd probably need an x-ray to find out for sure

345
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:54,980
Wow, you are super pale

346
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:57,300
Is that callous from writing too much?

347
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:58,200
Yeah

348
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:01,020
It's crazy that your hands are bigger than mine

349
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:02,280
What?

350
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:03,560
Why is that crazy?

351
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:06,540
I thought they were smaller for some reason

352
00:16:06,540 --> 00:16:17,300
I like you

353
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:19,340
Your hands

354
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:22,000
I really like your hands

355
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,340
They're nice and soft

356
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:24,180
They are?

357
00:16:24,580 --> 00:16:26,640
Yeah, and my thoughts were so loud they just came out

358
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:29,640
Maybe it's because I hold my pencil the right way

359
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:31,900
I don't have calluses like you do

360
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:33,580
Hey, that was uncalled for

361
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:36,040
Well, cool

362
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:38,760
And same

363
00:16:38,760 --> 00:16:41,560
I like yours, too

364
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:41,960
Yeah?

365
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:46,020
I like your hands

366
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:48,780
You said that already

367
00:16:48,780 --> 00:16:50,720
Yeah

368
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:53,740
I'm back!

369
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:55,440
Hey, welcome home

370
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:57,080
Have you washed your hands, Sota?

371
00:16:57,660 --> 00:16:58,420
Not yet

372
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:00,540
What's with the DVD, bro?

373
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:03,000
Hori was being a bit of a scatterbrain

374
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,240
And put them in the wrong cases

375
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:05,620
So I'm swapping them out

376
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:10,640
Hey, hurry and wash up

377
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:11,780
It's nearly dinner time

378
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:12,380
Okay

379
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:13,900
Oh, Miyamoto

380
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:15,820
Were you planning on eating with us tonight?

381
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,100
Uh, yeah

382
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:18,360
I was

383
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:21,260
Then go show Sota the meaning of the word clean

384
00:17:21,260 --> 00:17:22,440
You got it

385
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:23,220
Come on

386
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:24,260
Let's go

387
00:17:24,260 --> 00:17:25,100
Mm-hmm

388
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:39,480
Then she suddenly got all defensive

389
00:17:39,480 --> 00:17:42,440
She said Miyamoto's hers and Remy can't have him

390
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:42,780
What?

391
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:45,260
I was just joking around with her, of course

392
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:47,320
But Hori got super mad

393
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:50,280
Well, not the first time you took a joke too far

394
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:51,280
But still

395
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:53,040
Hori's scary

396
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:55,740
She's one girl you don't want to cross

397
00:17:55,740 --> 00:18:04,580
Hi, Miyamoto

398
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:05,340
What's up?

399
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:07,960
Nothing much

400
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:10,640
What the heck happened to your face?

401
00:18:12,020 --> 00:18:13,000
I got punched

402
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,000
And wound up fighting with someone

403
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:15,480
What?

404
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:16,960
You got in a fight

405
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:17,720
But with who?

406
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:19,820
Ishikawa

407
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:21,060
You're kidding me

408
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:22,980
I mean, sure, he's a big dummy dum-dum

409
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:24,960
But I never thought he'd throw down with a friend

410
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:26,520
Uh, Hori

411
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:28,320
Actually, the truth is

412
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:29,200
I don't want to hear it

413
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:30,840
Actions speak louder

414
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:33,880
And this action says all I need to know about what kind of guy he is

415
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:34,080
Huh?

416
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:35,480
Morning, Ishikawa

417
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:36,000
Bro

418
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,040
Holy shit

419
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:37,920
Toru?

420
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:39,220
Uh-huh

421
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:40,300
You called?

422
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:41,260
Huh?

423
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:42,820
Mm-hmm

424
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:47,400
Was it like a fist fight?

425
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:48,840
Yeah

426
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,900
So, you just punched each other

427
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:54,260
No, I dodged everything except that first punch

428
00:18:54,260 --> 00:18:56,540
So I guess fist fight might not be the right word

429
00:18:56,540 --> 00:18:59,720
More like I beat him to a bloody pulp

430
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:02,160
Remind me to never get on your bad side

431
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:03,880
Why were you fighting?

432
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:07,640
It's none of your business, Hori

433
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:08,780
Okay

434
00:19:08,780 --> 00:19:12,780
I guess I'm just having a hard time picturing this whole thing play out

435
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:16,960
Will you at least tell me who won?

436
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:18,580
Or is that top secret too?

437
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:21,500
That's quite a look

438
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:23,580
Excuse me

439
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:26,200
Pretty sure I lost

440
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:27,040
Big time

441
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:33,120
All I'm saying is I don't see it happening, dude

442
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:34,080
Hmm

443
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:36,720
Will you please take this seriously and listen?

444
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:38,800
You said something's not happening, right?

445
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,580
Hori obviously fell for you

446
00:19:41,580 --> 00:19:45,320
You're as wrong now as you were the first time you said that

447
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:47,300
It's your imagination

448
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:48,500
It's not

449
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:50,940
What if

450
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:53,320
I knew that it was the truth?

451
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:54,720
Some kind of test?

452
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:58,320
If Hori walked in here at this very moment and totally confessed to you

453
00:19:58,320 --> 00:19:59,520
What would your response be?

454
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:01,720
Would you still brush it off?

455
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:06,500
It doesn't matter because she just sees me as a friend

456
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:09,420
Why keep falling back on that lame-ass answer?

457
00:20:09,740 --> 00:20:12,240
Because you keep asking me the same lame-ass question

458
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:13,680
True

459
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:16,120
You said it's obvious she likes me

460
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:18,500
But I'd argue it's more obvious she doesn't

461
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:19,620
So what are you saying?

462
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:20,240
Well

463
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:22,940
Your feelings are involved

464
00:20:22,940 --> 00:20:25,800
And they're having a huge impact on the truth you accept

465
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:28,860
But you can't assume how Hori feels without asking

466
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:30,220
Look here!

467
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:34,960
You startled me so my reflexes took over

468
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,840
Let's see your reflexes handle this

469
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:37,660
What?

470
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:41,280
How the hell did we go for talking about feelings to you threatening me?

471
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:42,880
I guess push came to shove

472
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:43,640
What's that mean?

473
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:44,180
It means

474
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:45,260
Oh shit

475
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:46,160
Sorry

476
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,260
That hurt

477
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:50,980
Mercy, mercy

478
00:20:50,980 --> 00:20:53,060
Stop me about him, please

479
00:20:53,060 --> 00:21:01,700
It was self-defense

480
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:03,380
It's self-defense my ass

481
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:06,460
Completely uncalled for and irrelevant to Hori is what it was

482
00:21:06,460 --> 00:21:09,960
All this because I startled you?

483
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:11,180
Not quite

484
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:13,500
I was also really pissed off

485
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:14,360
Okay, man

486
00:21:14,360 --> 00:21:16,780
If you're trying to intimidate me, mission accomplished

487
00:21:16,780 --> 00:21:19,440
It's my fault

488
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:21,840
I pushed Miyamoto past his breaking point

489
00:21:21,840 --> 00:21:24,440
I feel so bad

490
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:25,680
Then it's settled

491
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:27,680
So go apologize already

492
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:31,940
Well

493
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:36,140
Miyamoto told me he's the reason both of them got so banged up and bruised

494
00:21:36,140 --> 00:21:36,620
What?

495
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:38,560
Toru says it's his fault

496
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:40,820
They fight and then they both want the blame

497
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:42,580
Weirdos

498
00:21:42,580 --> 00:21:43,520
I know

499
00:21:43,520 --> 00:21:45,780
I mean, geez

500
00:21:45,780 --> 00:21:47,480
Why even fight in the first place?

501
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:52,000
Please don't tell anyone

502
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,940
But we were fighting about Hori

503
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:55,900
It got intense

504
00:21:55,900 --> 00:22:00,740
What's so funny?

505
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:03,460
It is kind of cool, though

506
00:22:03,460 --> 00:22:05,160
How guys just duke it out

507
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:05,940
lol

508
00:22:05,940 --> 00:22:07,220
It sure is

509
00:22:23,740 --> 00:22:24,800
Wantmore

510
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:26,180
For 16 years

511
00:22:26,180 --> 00:22:27,820
For 16 years

512
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:29,160
I've seen my dream

513
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:31,040
The light inside

514
00:22:31,040 --> 00:22:36,040
綺麗な夜に

515
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:39,040
また明日ねと

516
00:22:39,040 --> 00:22:43,040
手を振る君の姿が

517
00:22:43,040 --> 00:22:48,040
名残惜しくって

518
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:51,040
長袖のシャツに

519
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:54,040
見覚えある道

520
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:59,040
少し寂しそうに見えた

521
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:03,040
胸が苦しくなるけど

522
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:06,040
暖かい

523
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:08,040
気づいた

524
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:12,040
冬の朝だ

525
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:17,040
約束するよ

526
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:20,040
近くにいるから

527
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:24,040
見えないものほど

528
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:29,040
大事にするよ

529
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:35,040
言葉にできないんだけどね

530
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:44,040
気づいた

531
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:46,040
気づいた

532
